<title>FRANCE: Dassault Electronique wins French army contract.</title>
<headline>Dassault Electronique wins French army contract.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>French aerospace electronics firm Dassault Electronique said on Monday it won a contract of unspecified value to equip light helicopters for the French army with FRUIT radar alert detectors.</p>
<p>A spokeswoman said the firm was prevented by military secrecy requirements from releasing the amount of the contract or the number of helicopters to be equipped with the lightweight devices, which she said were the most compact on the market.</p>
<p>But she said &quot;a large number&quot; of the army's 250 helicopters were involved.</p>
<p>Dassault Electronique said it beat out Thomson-CSF in competition for the contract.</p>
<p>(( -- Paris newsroom (33 1) 4221 5452 ))</p>
